  "plan": "Based on the feature description and previous Q&A, here is the implementation plan:\n\n## 1. Config Schema Changes\n\n### Add to <project_root>/.mad.config.json:\n- `code_path`: string (absolute path to project root)\n- `context_file`: string (path to CONTEXT.md, defaults to <project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md)\n- Resolve symlinks at read time using os.path.realpath()\n\n### Per-Board Configuration:\n- Store per-board config in <project_root>/.mad/boards/<boardname>/config.json\n- Per-board config takes precedence over global config (no merge, direct override)\n- Allow code_path to be set per-board; fall back to a default derivation if not set\n\n## 2. CONTEXT.md File Handling\n\n- Location: <project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md\n- Optional: missing file is OK, just ignore\n- Max size: 100KB - truncate at byte boundary (not character boundary) to avoid UTF-8 corruption\n- If file cannot be read (permission denied, etc.), ignore silently\n\n## 3. Agent Working Directory\n\n- When invoking an agent, set the working directory (cwd) to the project root (code_path), not the work item directory\n- This is a behavioral change from current implementation where cwd is set to the board's item location\n\n## 4. Agent Instructions Prepending\n\n- For each new agent session, prepend the following to the initial instruction prompt:\n  - \"Code Path: <code_path>\"\n  - \"Context File: <project_root>/.mad/CONTEXT.md\"\n- This applies to new agent sessions, not every message turn\n- If CONTEXT.md doesn't exist, still include the path in instructions\n\n## 5. CLI Commands (Required)\n\nImplement the following CLI commands:\n- `mad config set code_path <path>` - Set code_path in <project_root>/.mad.config.json\n- `mad config get code_path` - Get current code_path value\n- `mad context edit` - Edit CONTEXT.md using $EDITOR or fall back to a default editor\n- `mad context view` - Display current CONTEXT.md content (or indicate if missing)\n\n## 6. Default Code Path Derivation\n\n- Default: Allow derivation from board location as fallback\n- Algorithm: Use board directory's parent.parent (board's parent is <boardname>, parent's parent is project root)\n- If code_path doesn't exist (new project), allow it - don't validate existence at config write time\n\n## 7. Implementation Steps\n\n1. Modify config loading to read from <project_root>/.mad.config.json\n2. Add code_path and context_file fields to config schema\n3. Implement per-board config loading with precedence\n4. Create CONTEXT.md file handling functions (read, write with truncation, ignore errors)\n5. Modify agent invocation to set cwd to code_path\n6. Add instruction prepending for new agent sessions\n7. Implement CLI commands: config set/get, context edit/view\n8. Add error handling for config write failures (permissions, disk full)\n9. Handle editor fallback ($EDITOR, then vim, then error)\n\n## 8. Security Considerations (Future Item)\n\n- Document that setting cwd to project root has security implications if agent runs malicious code\n- Path validation to prevent escaping to parent directories or accessing sensitive paths is noted for future consideration but not implemented now"
